AR):L6":{"b":"BARDEN (STAR)","p":"L6"},"PBC LINEAR:FLR06":{"b":"PBC LINEAR","p":"FLR06"},"THOMSON:SUPER-6":{"b":"THOMSON","p":"SUPER-6","s":{"Features":"<ul><li>A coefficient of friction as low as 0.001 and allows the use of smaller, less expensive motors, belts, gears and ball screws when replacing high-friction, plain bearings</li><li>A self-aligning capability up to 0.5 deg compensates for inaccuracies in base flatness or carriage machining</li><li>Accelerations as high as 150 m/sq-s and steady state travel speeds up to 3 m/s without the derating factors commonly required with linear guides</li><li>Double-lip integral wipers that keep out dirt while retaining lubrication and travel life is maximized</li><li>Lightweight, wear-resistant, engineered polymer retainers and outer sleeves that reduce inertia and noise</li><li>The Super Ball Bushing&reg; bearing is self-aligning, lightweight and adjustable with a low coefficient of friction</li><li>The wear-resistant, engineered-polymer retainers and outer sleeves reduce inertia and noise in critical, high speed applications</li><li>Radially floating bearing plates when installed in an adjustable housing, the Super Ball Bushing&reg; bearing may be adjusted to a specific diametrical fit-up for accurate and repeatable movement</li><li>Self-aligning</li></ul>","Images":"https://externalassets.unilogcorp.com/ASSETS/IMAGES/ITEMS/ORIGINAL_HIGHRES/Thomson_SUPER10_1.jpg | https://externalassets.unilogcorp.com/ASSETS/IMAGES/ITEMS/ORIGINAL_HIGHRES/Thomson_SPM12.jpg","PDF":"https://externalassets.unilogcorp.com/ASSETS/DOCUMENTS/ITEMS/EN/Thomson_FNYBU06_Catalog.pdf Thomson_FNYBU06_Catalog.pdf","Bearing Material":"Steel","Length":"7/8 in","Load Capacity":"100 lb Dynamic","Maximum Speed":"3 m/s","Outside Diameter":"5/8 in","Shaft Diameter":"3/8 in","Temperature Rating":"185 deg F","Type":"Adjustable Closed","WEIGHT":"0.04 lb"}},"THOMSON:SS6U-8":{"b":"THOMSON","p":"SS6U-8","s":{"Features":"<ul><li>A precision, super finished, dual track bearing plate for optimum system smoothness and performance</li><li>Longer travel life and minimal machine downtime when replacing conventional linear bearings or the industry standard Super Ball Bushing&reg; bearing</li><li>RoundRail&trade; advantage combined with universal self-alignment, eliminating the need for derating factors commonly required when using linear guides</li><li>A coefficient of friction as low as 0.001 and allows the use of smaller, less expensive motors, belts, gears and ball screws when replacing high-friction, plain bearings</li><li>Double-lip integral wipers that keep out dirt while retaining lubrication and travel life is maximized</li><li>Steady state travel speeds up to 10 ft/s and accelerations to 450 ft/s without the use of derating factors</li><li>The bearing plate is designed to rock 0.5 deg about the hardened precision ground outer ring</li><li>The second key design feature of the Super Smart Ball Bushing&reg; bearing plate is its ability to roll</li><li>The shape formed by the rock and roll features allows the Super Smart Ball Bushing&reg; bearing plate to rotate about its center</li><li>The Super Smart Ball Bushing&reg; bearing provides twice the load capacity of the industry standard Thomson&reg; Super Ball Bushing&reg; bearing and six times the load capacity of conventional linear bearings</li><li>The Super Smart Ball Bushing&reg; bearing provides eight times the travel life of the industry standard Thomson&reg; Super Ball Bushing&reg; bearing and 216 times the travel life of conventional linear bearings</li><li>Its unique design with the steel band enables the bearing to preserve it&apos;s ID fit-up and self-aligning capability over extended use</li><li>A universal self-alignment feature optimizes load distribution between ball tracks and assures uniform ball loading over the entire length of the bearing plate</li><li>This patented product provides smooth, quiet, low drag linear movement at 6x the load capacity or 216 x the L10 travel life of a conventional steel linear ball bushing bearing</li><li>These universally self-aligning bearings offer twice the load capacity or eight times the travel life of our Super Ball Bushing&reg; bearing</li><li>For class L, end supported shafting</li><li>Self-aligning</li><li>No wipers</li></ul>","Images":"https://externalassets.unilogcorp.com/ASSETS/IMAGES/ITEMS/ORIGINAL_HIGHRES/Thomson_SS6U8.jpg | https://externalassets.unilogcorp.com/ASSETS/IMAGES/ITEMS/ORIGINAL_HIGHRES/Thomson_SS6U8_1.jpg","PDF":"https://externalassets.unilogcorp.com/ASSETS/DOCUMENTS/ITEMS/EN/Thomson_FNYBU06_Catalog.pdf Thomson_FNYBU06_Catalog.pdf","Bearing Material":"Steel","Length":"1-1/4 in","Load Capacity":"265 lb Dynamic","Outside Diameter":"7/8 in","Shaft Diameter":"1/2 in","Temperature Rating":"185 deg F","Type":"Adjustable Closed","WEIGHT":"0.1 lb"}},"THOMSON:A-81420":{"b":"THOMSON","p":"A-81420","s":{"Features":"<ul><li>The RoundRail&trade; advantage which minimizes installation time and cost</li><li>Steady state travel speeds up to 10 ft/s and accelerations to 450 ft/sq-s without the use of derating factors</li><li>An operating temperature up to 600 deg F/315 deg C</li><li>Replace high-friction plain bearings</li><li>Lasting precision alignment</li><li>High travel speeds</li><li>Ease of installation</li><li>Protection from contamination</li><li>Precision steel Ball Bushing&reg; bearings offer great improvements in efficiency, productivity and accuracy over high friction plain bearings flat-ways</li><li>The all steel design makes the bearing product line perfect for replacing plain bearings in high temperature applications</li><li>The steel sleeve anti-friction recirculating ball bushing provides rigid low drag movement 100x lower drag coefficient than a plain contact bearing</li><li>A coefficient of friction as low as 0.001 when replacing high friction plain bearings, Precision Steel Ball Bushing&reg; bearings dramatically improve machine productivity and efficiency</li><li